---
/**
 * Analytics.astro — mounts the PII-safe analytics runtime
 * (`src/lib/analytics-runtime.ts`) on every page via `BaseLayout.astro`.
 *
 * **Opus gate B3 (blocking): "Ship the Analytics script as a bundled
 * external file, never `is:inline`."** This is now a plain, non-inline
 * `<script>` — Astro hoists it into an external, same-origin, hashed
 * bundle (`dist/_astro/Analytics.astro_astro_type_script_….js`), exactly
 * like `CourseMap.astro`/`SiteSearch.astro`/`BaseLayout.astro`'s own
 * scripts, so it runs under this site's `default-src 'self'` CSP with no
 * `'unsafe-inline'` exception. The PREVIOUS stage-2 design kept this
 * component real-but-unmounted with an `is:inline` script (extracted for
 * testing via a `vm`-sandbox + regex, never actually shipped anywhere) —
 * that shape is gone; see `analytics-runtime.ts`'s module doc for the
 * full reasoning and `test/analytics-pii.test.ts` for how the module is
 * tested directly now instead.
 *
 * **Still inert without a GTM container** (O13, stage-2 scope item 6:
 * "Keep the GTM slot empty. The container ID comes from build config
 * later.") — `installAnalytics()` returns immediately when
 * `window.dataLayer` doesn't exist, which it never will until BaseLayout
 * actually injects a GTM snippet (still not done — no such snippet exists
 * anywhere in this codebase). Mounting this component ships the PII
 * BOUNDARY, not a live analytics integration.
 */
---

<script>
  import { installAnalytics } from "../lib/analytics-runtime";
  installAnalytics();
</script>
